---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Sportivo Public Fixture API | Developer Documentation" description="Public fixture API documentation for Sportivo by Dipesh Sapkota." canonical="https://sportivo.dipeshsapkota7.com.np/api-docs/">
  <SiteHeader /><main class="site-shell min-h-screen text-slate-100"><article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-20 pt-12"><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-xs text-slate-500"><a href="/">Sportivo</a><span class="mx-2">/</span><span>Developer documentation</span></nav><h1 class="mt-10 text-4xl font-black text-white sm:text-6xl">Sportivo Public Fixture API</h1><p class="mt-6 leading-8 text-slate-300">Sportivo provides public read-only fixture endpoints. Data is dynamic and supplied by the upstream provider.</p><h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-black text-white">Endpoints</h2><ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 text-slate-300"><li><code>GET /api/matches/football</code></li><li><code>GET /api/matches/cricket</code></li><li><code>GET /api/matches/basketball</code></li></ul><h2 class="mt-12 text-2xl font-black text-white">Response contract</h2><p class="mt-4 leading-8 text-slate-300">Successful responses are JSON arrays. A fixture may contain title or name, category, status, time fields, teams, poster or image, and sources. Clients must tolerate missing fields, empty arrays, provider changes, and unavailable streams.</p><p class="mt-8 text-slate-400">Created and published by <a class="text-[#c9f36b]" href="https://www.dipeshsapkota7.com.np/">Dipesh Sapkota</a>.</p></article></main>
</BaseLayout>